        "en": "Matrix powers describe a theoretical law; counts from one fixed seed describe an empirical path. A finite grid may remove rare transitions and destroy connectivity of Q. Tiny coupling can leave displayed probabilities identical while contraction and nonreversible flow remain nonzero, so inspect retained numerical bounds."
