        "en": "With fixed A,h,c the classical quadratic model retains C/kB=1 at every positive temperature. Its density narrows, differential entropy tends to minus infinity and the limiting point mass is not the original area density. A finite-gap ground law and zero heat capacity belong to a different preparation and reference measure."
