        "en": "At a=b=0 every initial law is stationary and is its own pointwise limit; do not choose a single reference arbitrarily. At a=0,b>0, state zero absorbs and every start converges to the unique stationary law. The reverse-transition row at zero stationary mass is unavailable. A constant indicator has zero variance and covariance but unavailable normalized correlation."
