        "en": "The Cesaro mean here averages N+1 probability laws from mu_0 through mu_N. For exact alternation, mean state-one probability is 1/3 at N=2 and 1/2 at N=3. The latter equals the stationary law while the final law is concentrated at state one. This is not a random sample-mean variance or ESS calculation."
